Both are licensed under the Apache License 2.0. `make setup` downloads them into upstream/ and
copies their LICENSE into every upload folder. Converted ONNX graphs are derivatives of these
model weights and remain subject to that license.

src/moederncolbert_onnx/portable.py adapts the upstream inference architecture into tensor-only
operations for ONNX. Changes include explicit attention, 512-position RoPE buffers, dense
evaluation of every routed expert with the learned top-k gating, and inclusion of the separate
projection head and normalization. That adapted file is distributed under Apache-2.0. The other
original project code is distributed under MIT (LICENSE).

Dependencies retain their own licenses. ONNX Runtime files copied by the demo build are subject to
ONNX Runtime's license (third-party/ONNXRUNTIME-LICENSE.txt).
